SUMMARY:Jingle Bell Rockin' Tribute Band
DESCRIPTION:A Tribute to Bobby Helms and His Christmas Classic “Jingle Bell Rock” with Special Guest: The Isaac Family Band. \nWhen country music singer Bobby Helms was first offered the chance to sing a new festive song called “Jingle Bell Rock\,” he was initially skeptical about the idea of mixing rock’n’roll and Christmas. But he was quickly won over\, and his single\, issued by Decca Records in October 1957\, soon became a holiday classic. “‘Jingle Bell Rock’ has made itself a part of Christmas\,” Helms said. “It lifts people up.” Today\, you can find it on playlists alongside staples like “Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer\,” Nat King Cole’s “The Christmas Song\,” \n\nBUY TICKETS
URL:https://browncountyplayhouse.org/event/jingle-bell-rockin-tribute-band-2026/
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S. Van Buren St\, Nashville\, IN\, 47448\, United States
CATEGORIES:Blues,Clasic Rock,Featured Event,Music,Pop Rock
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncountyplayhouse.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2026-jinglebell_web_event.jpg
END:VEVENT
